@meta
id: 23-12
title: Drill — next typo, first suggestion
chapter: 23
type: drill
skills: spell
par: 22
minutes: 3
reps: 8
vscode: hover each squiggle, click the fix
open: standup.md
vimrc: set spell

@brief
Three typos in three lines. Eight times: jump to each and take the
first suggestion. Never look for the typo yourself and never type the
correction.

@keys
| `]s` | next misspelled word |
| `1z=` | first suggestion |

@hints
`]s` then `1z=`, three times over.
--
You do not need to read the file. `]s` knows where the typos are.

@solution
    ]s1z= ]s1z= ]s1z= :wq<Enter>

Nineteen keystrokes. After a few reps `]s1z=` is one motion in your
hand, and that is the state to be in for commit messages and docs:
write, then sweep.

@start standup.md
Yesterday: shipped the refund fix and updated the relase notes.
Today: reviewing the payments PR and tidying the enviroment variables.
Blocked: waiting on finance to confirm the thirty day window is definately final.

@expected standup.md
Yesterday: shipped the refund fix and updated the release notes.
